o  sensei not one of his current students  mind you but a former fanboy who looked  up to tentacle guy for his killing ways  this is the reaper or reaper 2.0 as he's  called years after taking on goro  sensei's mantle the reaper finally got  his chance to bring down goro sensei for  good unleashing his final form  a sinister looks similar to the friendly  yellow teacher we've come to love along  with the sinister form comes sinister  power  the overwhelmed goro sensei at the start  reaper would have won had he not made  one big mistake harming one of goro  sensei's dear students  this ultimately leads to his doom but at  least he has a claim to fame of being  able to knock around the seemingly  invincible koro sensei  following that we have midoriya and  vaguely versus all might  going up against the world's number one  hero for a final exam is no easy task  even if there's two of you how about  doing so as a pair of rivals who at  times just can't stand each other at  this point you gotta wonder which is  harder  be in all might or actually learning how  to work together the latter proves to be  an insane challenge for the team of  midori and bakugou it takes a while but  they eventually get some of it done  bakugo's all-out attacks aren't as  effective as expected but it's  midoriya's save that proves to be  instrumental in determining the result  of the exam  in truth this wasn't a battle of  strength despite it being hyped as a  collision course of powerful forces the  actual fighting was never the point to  begin with it was a test of willpower  and mindset  and the two prospective heroes passed  the test with flying colours  [Music]  finishing up the list is chiron vs  achilles  as much as the face series has epic  fights i always felt that it lacked the  student teacher dynamic in the mainline  series it's not a big loss or anything  like that but i felt that having this  kind of story backdrop would be epic in  something like the fate series  well apocrypha 